### 3. Microwave Radio Link YANG Model
* **Presentation:** [02 - A YANG Data Model for Microwave Radio Link](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ccamp-02-a-yang-data-model-for-microwave-radio-link-00)
* **Presenter:** Jonas Ahlberg
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-ccamp-rfc8561bis`
* **Discussion:**
  * The document has been adopted as `draft-ietf-ccamp-rfc8561bis` to replace RFC 8561 and moved to the IETF CCAMP GitHub repository.
  * **Reference Modulation Scheme:** Replaced spectral efficiency clause with "reference modulation index" to align with ETSI EN 302 217.
  * **Band and Carrier Aggregation:** A pull request is under review to support mixing carriers on different frequency bands and capacities (distinct from traditional bonding).
  * **Radio Link Terminal (RLT) Mode:** Proposed making `RLT mode` a read-only leaf to prevent configuration conflicts with individual constituent carrier configurations.
  * **Other Features:** Ongoing work on space diversity, cross-polarization across multiple nodes (XPIC), and evaluation of loopback placement (radio link vs. Ethernet layer).
  * **Receiver Control:** Vendor and operator feedback was requested regarding use cases for disabling individual receivers (`Rx enabled`).
  * Luis M. Contreras suggested sending an informational liaison to ETSI as the alignment progresses.

