### 4. Optical Pluggables Gap Analysis
* **Presentation:** [03 - Data Modelling and Gap Analysis of Optical Pluggables in Packet Over Optical Network](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ccamp-03-data-modelling-and-gap-analysis-of-optical-pluggables-in-packet-over-optical-network-00)
* **Presenter:** Nigel Davis
* **Discussion:**
  * The team concluded that line-side photonic properties of pluggables are independent of form factor and should be integrated into existing optical models (e.g., `draft-ietf-ccamp-dwdm-if-param-yang`) rather than creating standalone pluggable YANG models.
  * Line-side gap analysis is near completion. Remaining work focuses on host-to-plug interface properties (power, lane configuration) and external capability metadata handling.
  * Fatai Zhang clarified the interaction between host/line models and pluggable attributes; Nigel Davis confirmed no standalone line-side pluggable model is being created.

