### 5. CMIS Access and Control
* **Presentation:** [04 - A YANG Data Model for CMIS Access and Control](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ccamp-04-a-yang-data-model-for-cmis-access-and-control-00)
* **Presenter:** Shoichi Sakeno
* **Discussion:**
  * Defines a YANG model mirroring the CMIS memory map for attributes not abstracted by host Network Operating Systems (NOS), keeping the host NOS NETCONF server in the control loop.
  * **v04 Updates:** Introduced opt-in page delegation, clear handover rules between host NOS and external controller, non-delegable critical registers (lower memory, CDB pages), rate-limited RPCs/actions, and phased deployment recommendations. Prototype implementation is underway on open-source SONiC.
  * **Future v05 Plan:** Embed delegation constraints directly into YANG schema rules and unify error handling between RPCs and actions.
  * **Comments & Feedback:**
    * Fatai Zhang raised bank-granular access control scenarios (e.g., allocating specific banks/lanes to remote controllers).
    * Nigel Davis inquired about handling CMIS reset-on-read and time-critical counters (to be discussed on the mailing list).
    * Italo Busi and Nigel Davis recommended splitting the work into a problem statement draft and a solution draft, and sharing the problem statement with OIF.
    * Authors requested a Working Group adoption call for the draft.

