### 7. NMA Integration into ACTN Architecture
* **Presentation:** [06 - Integration of Network Management Agent (NMA) into ACTN-Based Optical Network](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ccamp-06-integration-of-network-management-agent-nma-into-actn-based-optical-network-00)
* **Presenter:** De Xiao
* **Draft Context:** `draft-ietf-ccamp-actn-optical-transport-mgmt`
* **Discussion:**
  * Proposes integrating AI/LLM-based Network Management Agents (NMAs) into ACTN entities (CNC, MDSC, PNC) for autonomous closed-loop operation without altering underlying ACTN control roles.
  * Introduces an Agent Proxy for capability aggregation/registration across multiple agents, logical Agent-to-Agent (A2A) interactions, and extended MPI capabilities.
  * **Security & Control:** Reuses ACTN security primitives; requires manual approval/human-in-the-loop for high-risk changes; mandates that configuration changes be executed through predefined templates rather than direct LLM command generation.
  * **Comments:** Daniel King highlighted potential issues regarding race conditions, state divergence, and agent conflicts, recommending coordination with the ICON (Control and Intervention) group on observability and control primitives.
  * Authors requested WG adoption.

