### 8. SLA Assurance Management in Optical Transport Networks
* **Presentation:** [07 - A YANG Data Model for Service Level Agreement (SLA) Assurance Management in Optical Transport Networks](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ccamp-07-a-yang-data-model-for-service-level-agreement-sla-assurance-management-in-optical-transport-networks-00)
* **Presenter:** Henry Yu
* **Discussion:**
  * Refined the definition of "Service Assurance Issue" as a detected optical network condition (e.g., shared trench) affecting SLA fulfillment that may exist without immediate customer-visible impact or associated incidents.
  * Clarified distinction from SAIN (Service Assurance for Intent-based Networking): SAIN models service health, whereas this model provides optical-specific physical dependency data.
  * Clarified protection path latency issues: specified that latency degradation stems from physical protection path distance rather than switching operation latency.
  * Detailed ACTN interworking (PNC reporting domain-level observations to MDSC).
  * Section 4.4.6 outlines open issues for community input: issue-to-service correlation, issue type classifications, statistical semantics, SFP export definitions, and resolution capabilities.

