### 9. Fine-Grain OTN (fgOTN) YANG Data Models
* **Presentation:** [08 - YANG Data Models for fine grain Optical Transport Network](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ccamp-08-yang-data-models-for-fine-grain-optical-transport-network-01)
* **Presenter:** Yan Xia
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-ccamp-fgotn-yang`
* **Discussion:**
  * Updated to revision 03 following adoption as `draft-ietf-ccamp-fgotn-yang`.
  * **Topology Model:** Removed custom FGOTN bandwidth lists; reused IETF OTN `odu-list` structures from `draft-ietf-ccamp-otn-tunnel-model` and introduced `fg-odu-flex` in fgOTN types. Provided a step-by-step bandwidth allocation example in Appendix B.
  * **Label Restrictions:** Replaced integer string definitions with strong data types (`uint8`/`uint16`) and added a `when` clause restricting label restrictions to tributary slot (TS) ranges.
  * **Tunnel & Types Models:** Set `fg-odu-flex` bandwidth type to `uint8` (1 to 192) per ITU-T G.709; split TS types into `ts-list` (for tunnel hop) and `ts-list-or-empty` (for topology range); encapsulated TS numbers into `fg-ts-number-grouping`.
  * Next steps include addressing GitHub open issues, completing management considerations, and adding tunnel JSON examples.

